{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LUduMvqzPuxRecezskw6GM","type":"tool_result","content":"150:- Insight: `package_name` = the `<manifest package=...>` attribute (the applicationId), verbatim -- NOT the label, NOT\n151:  the filename (`mobile-001` is the \"friendly filename\"), NOT `.MainActivity`'s expanded class. Clones/rebuilds/borrowed\n152:  label = signer cert, versionCode and `android:label` -- not asked yet.\n153:- Tools: `aapt dump badging f.apk | head -1` (first line answers it); androguard `APK(data, raw=True).get_package()`;\n154:  pure stdlib AXML walk (string pool UTF-16/UTF-8 flag 0x100, START_ELEMENT 0x0102, 20-B attributes; `package` has no\n155:  resource id, so look it up by NAME). No `apk` fmt in `lib.meta` -> race probe returned nothing; the live worker\n156:  answered. Ratchet folds `lib/meta/apk.py` (stdlib walk + androguard fallback).\n157:- Single first submit CORRECT ~32 s (no wrong). TT 26 / Mastery 130 CORRECT in-window first try (the seeded solver\n158:  already had `local_answer` + synthesis dispatch; the worker only added the apk branch).\n159:\n160:## GM answer conventions learned\n161:- Filenames: exact base name incl. extension, no directory. Sizes: base-10 integer, no units. Hashes: hex, case ignored.\n162:- Byte prefixes: lowercase hex, contiguous, exactly 2N chars (`xxd -p -l N`). Booleans: enum `true` / `false`.\n163:- Pixel dimensions (JPEG SOF, PNG IHDR, video `media.primary_video_dimensions` D18): `<width>x<height>`, lowercase\n164:  `x`, no spaces. Video = ffprobe width/height of v:0 (coded size, NOT rotated, not the tkhd display size).\n165:- PDF header version: bare `x.y`; absent -> literal `none` (wording; `none` not yet GM-confirmed). Counts: plain integer.\n166:- JSON lists -- compact, double quotes, no spaces; ORDER depends on the field:\n167:  - `zip.central_directory_member_names`: full stored paths in CD order (`[\"room-01/item-1.txt\",\"room-02/item-1.txt\"]`).\n168:  - `ooxml.external_relationship_targets`: Target strings SORTED ascending (D15 all modes); rels-file order REJECTED.\n169:  - `*-synthesis-<algo>-order`: member names ordered by hex digest ascending (D15-D20 TT/Mastery; `case_insensitive`).\n170:  - `macho.cpu_type_set`: `[\"0x%08x\", ...]` one per slice; thin = one element (D20). Fat: fat_arch order (unverified).\n171:  Heuristic: a list read off one on-disk structure that the field name calls \"names in the directory\" keeps disk\n172:  order; a set gathered across parts (\"targets\", \"dependencies\") is sorted. If an order is rejected, try the other.\n173:- Header integers as hex (`*_hex`): `0x` + lowercase hex ZERO-PADDED to the struct field's width: u16 PE Machine\n174:  `0x014c`, u16 ELF e_machine `0x003e` (D19), u32 AddressOfEntryPoint `0x00065bd0`, u32 Mach-O cputype `0x0100000c`\n175:  (D20, inside a JSON list, even without `_hex` in the id; ABI64 bit kept, no name). Width from the STRUCT / the\n176:  `_uNN_` in the id; the value from the file's own byte order (ELF EI_DATA). (Magic-prefix hex has NO `0x`; the\n177:  binary lane's machine wants `i386` and accepted unpadded entry points -- different generator.)\n178:- GUIDs: .NET MVID `Guid.ToString()` lowercase no braces (D12); MSI ProductCode the stored string uppercase WITH braces\n179:  (D13). Spelling follows the source, not answer_format.\n180:- Windows paths (`lnk.target_path_windows`): stored LinkInfo path verbatim (backslashes, case, drive letter, no quotes).\n181:- Android identifiers (`apk.package_name`, D21): the manifest `package` attribute verbatim (dotted, case kept, no\n182:  quotes, no version suffix). Same \"stored string verbatim\" rule as OriginalFilename / Message-ID.\n183:- Version-resource strings (`pe.version_<field>`): StringFileInfo value verbatim incl. extension.\n184:- URLs (`ooxml` Targets): the attribute value verbatim -- scheme, host, path as stored; no trailing-slash or case fixups.\n185:- E-mail headers (`email.<field>`): header value as stored after RFC 5322 unfolding; Message-ID WITH `<>` (D16).\n186:- Media codec names (`media.*codec_name`, D17): ffprobe `codec_name`: WAV tag 1 -> `pcm_u8`/`pcm_s16le`/`pcm_s24le`/\n187:  `pcm_s32le` by bits (RIFX `..be`), 3 `pcm_f32le`, 6 `pcm_alaw`, 7 `pcm_mulaw`, 0x55 `mp3`; only `pcm_s16le` verified.\n188:- Rejected spellings: `0x65bd0` (D10, unpadded); brace-less MSI GUID (D13); rels-file-order target list (D15);\n189:  bracket-less Message-ID (D16); `[\"arm64\"]` arch name for `macho.cpu_type_set` (D20). Pattern: delimiters that are part of the stored v\n190:- Inference: the field id IS the spec name (`sof_` = SOF header, `eocd_total_entries` = the EOCD's own claim,\n191:  `e_machine` = Elf_Ehdr member) -- read it literally to pick the structure. A claimed count is NOT a CD walk; CD\n192:  names are NOT local-header names; `_uNN_hex` fixes read+print width. Unverified ELF siblings: bare enum-ish fields\n193:  (`ei_data`, `e_type`) have no GM spelling yet -- lib emits `ELFDATA2LSB` / `2`; prefer the `_hex` form if offered.\n194:  D20 extends it: header CODES (machine, cputype, subtype, filetype) are emitted as raw `0x` hex, never as tool names.\n195:\n196:## Delivery layouts seen (resolve these before parsing)\n197:- Single / TT: one zip; members named in `artifact` after `->` (filename questions: artifact = the zip only). Mastery\n198:  (most days, all of D15-20): ONE download holding `-01.zip`..`-0N.zip` (D7 three levels; D15+ five full kits); refs\n199:  `<set zip> -> <member>`, names reused per set -> resolve by (set zip, member). D9: download `<id>-mastery.zip` vs refs\n200:  `...-evidence-0N.zip` -> resolve by sha256 (`lib.common.container_by_sha`). D6: two same-named downloads ->\n201:  `delivery N: <zip>` refs. Member numbering shifts between pre-fetched contract and live attempt -- never hardcode.\n202:\n203:## Pitfalls that cost time\n204:- **Synthesis dispatch lost AGAIN (D15, D16, D17, D19)**: every day the single's `solve.py` answers the new field but the\n205:  timed kit adds `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-sha256-order` -> `solver_incomplete` -> an offline generalize (~1 min per\n206:  mode). D18 was clean only because the single worker pre-wired it. Right after single CORRECT: `grep -n synthesis\n207:  solver/solve.py` must show a dispatch calling `lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order`, with the artifacts root set INSIDE\n208:  the per-set worker (`_solve_pairs`; Mastery forks one process per set), plus identity for ANY member stem and every\n209:  carry-over family. Start from the previous day's solver, not a fresh template. D20 + D21 were clean because the\n210:  lane seed (`local_answer` + `synthesis_answer` + `lib.meta.answer`) was used -- keep doing that.\n211:- Id-slug parsing (D16, 1 wrong): ids repeat the fmt word (`d16-email-001-email-message-id`); a regex on the first\n212:  `email-` yields `001-email-message-id` -> lookup miss -> `none`. Anchor `-\\d+-<fmt>-(.+)$`. Never submit `none`\n213:  without grepping the bytes for the field -- `none` means absent in the artifact, not \"my parser returned None\".\n214:- Registry misses (D14 key one suffix short `lnk.target_path`; D16 fmt `eml` vs GM `email`; D17 `wav.*` vs `media.*`):\n215:  `python3 -c \"import lib.meta as m; print([k for k in m.known_fields() if k[0]=='<fmt>'])\"` and grep\n216:  `lib/meta/prebuilt/*.py` for the FIELD name; call the nearest extractor directly. D18-D20 HIT the registry; D21\n217:  MISSED (prebuilt had `dex`/`jar`/`java` but no `apk` fmt) -> ~32 s LLM solve instead of ~5-13 s. A new CONTAINER\n218:  family (apk, ipa, aab, msix...) needs its own fmt word registered, not just its inner members. D20\n219:  substring trap: `cpu_type_set` fell into macho's scalar `cpu_type` branch -> bare hex where `json` wants a list --\n220:  check the SHAPE vs answer_format; `_set`/`_list`/`_names` = one entry per slice/member (wrap a thin value in `[...]`).\n221:- Endianness (D19 pun): never `struct.unpack('<H')` an ELF/Mach-O field blindly -