amp 0x6dff800d, verity padding 0x42726577, dependency/frosting ids verbatim), v1_signature_file_names (META-INF *.SF/*.RSA/*.DSA/*.EC in CD order), signer_cert_sha256 / signer_cert_sha1 / signer_cert_md5 (lowercase hex of the DER cert; also `:`-separated uppercase sibling `_colon` as apksigner/keytool print), signer_subject_dn / signer_issuer_dn (RFC 4514 string, also `_cn`), signer_serial_hex, signer_not_before_utc / not_after_utc, signer_public_key_sha256, signer_key_algorithm (RSA/EC/DSA), signer_key_bits, v2_signer_count, v1_v2_cert_match (true/false), manifest_mf_created_by. Locate the block: EOCD -> CD offset; 16 B before it = magic `APK Sig Block 42`, u64 size before that; pairs = u64 len + u32 id + value. v2/v3 signer: length-prefixed signed data -> digests, certificates (DER). v1: PKCS#7 SignedData DER in *.RSA -> certificates [0] -- hand DER walk (no cryptography/asn1crypto in the gate; pycryptodome Crypto.Util.asn1 is allowed). Shares the DER walker with x509-cert / pe-authenticode.\"},\n {\"id\":\"apk-label-resources-arsc\",\"concept\":\"Resolve `@string`/`@mipmap` references in the APK manifest through resources.arsc (the 'borrowed product name')\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D21 flavor 'expose the borrowed product name' = android:label (D21 label was an inline string 'Huntress Evidence <digits>'; a variant can make it a reference 0x7f0X....). fmt apk: application_label_resolved (default config value of the referenced string), application_label_raw (`@0x7f0b0001` style or the inline string), app_label_locales (JSON {locale: value} from every ResTable_config), resources_package_name (ResTable_package name UTF-16 128 chars @+12 -- may DIFFER from manifest package = a rebuilt/renamed clone), resources_package_id_hex (`0x7f`), icon_path (resolved res/... path). resources.arsc: RES_TABLE_TYPE 0x0002 -> global string pool -> package chunk 0x0200 {id u32, name[128] u16, typeStrings, keyStrings} -> TYPE_SPEC 0x0202 / TYPE 0x0201 chunks (config, entry offsets, ResTable_entry {size,flags,key} + Res_value). Ref 0xPPTTEEEE = package/type/entry (type and entry are 1-based / 0-based respectively). Prefer the default config (all-zero ResTable_config); else first. Stdlib struct only.\"},\n {\"id\":\"apk-clone-rebuild-synthesis\",\"concept\":\"Cross-APK clone vs rebuild synthesis (package id / signer / version / label)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Extend lib.meta.synthesis (fmt synthesis) for ids `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-<key>` whose question lists several .apk (or .ipa) members in `Files: [...]` (parse like digest_order; get_bytes per set). Keys to support by id slug / question words: package_groups (JSON object package -> sorted member names, or list of lists sorted by first name), signer_groups (by signer cert sha256), clone_members ('clone' = same package or same label, DIFFERENT signer than the earliest/lowest-versionCode member), rebuild_members ('rebuild' = same package AND same signer, different versionCode/APK digest), borrowed_label_member (label equal to another package's label), version_code_order (names ordered by versionCode asc, tie -> name), distinct_package_count. Emit compact JSON; names sorted ascending inside groups unless the question says otherwise. Uses apk-manifest-siblings + apk-signing-certs extractors; tolerate non-APK members (skip / `none`).\"},\n {\"id\":\"ios-ipa-identity\",\"concept\":\"iOS .ipa identity: Info.plist bundle fields, embedded.mobileprovision, main executable architecture\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D21 'Mobile packages' (plural) + the lane's one-family-per-day walk -> iOS next is plausible. fmt ipa (aliases ios, ios_app): zip with `Payload/<Name>.app/Info.plist` (binary `bplist00` or XML; reuse prebuilt plist parser). Fields: bundle_identifier (CFBundleIdentifier verbatim), bundle_short_version (CFBundleShortVersionString), bundle_version (CFBundleVersion), bundle_display_name, bundle_name, bundle_executable, minimum_os_version, platform_name / supported_platforms (CFBundleSupportedPlatforms JSON), device_family (UIDeviceFamily JSON ints), app_bundle_name (`<Name>.app`), executable_cpu_type_set (the CFBundleExecutable Mach-O: reuse macho cpu_type_set -> JSON list of `0x%08x`), executable_lc_uuid, has_mobileprovision, provision_team_identifier (TeamIdentifier[0]), provision_app_id_name, provision_uuid, provision_name, provision_expiration_utc, provision_creation_utc, provision_application_identifier (Entitlements application-identifier), provision_get_task_allow, provision_provisions_all_devices, provision_device_count. embedded.mobileprovision = CMS SignedData DER whose eContent is an XML plist: find `<?xml` .. `</plist>` in the bytes and plistlib-parse (no CMS walk needed). Also `iTunesMetadata.plist` (itemId, softwareVersionBundleId, artistName) if present.\"},\n {\"id\":\"apk-native-abis-dex\",\"concept\":\"APK payload inventory: native-lib ABI set, multidex count, per-dex header, resources/assets\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"fmt apk: native_abis (JSON sorted set of `lib/<abi>/` dirs: arm64-v8a, armeabi-v7a, armeabi, x86, x86_64, riscv64), native_lib_names (CD order), native_lib_e_machines_u16_hex (per .so via elf e_machine), abi_mismatch (dir ABI vs e_machine disagree -> member names), dex_count (classes.dex, classes2.dex, ...), dex_names, dex_versions (from `dex\\\\n0NN\\\\0`), classes_dex_sha256 / classes_dex_checksum_u32_hex (route into prebuilt dex fields for `classes.dex`), has_resources_arsc, asset_names, entry_count, cd_member_names (CD order), zip_alignment_ok (STORED entries data offset % 4 == 0; .so % 4096), duplicate_entry_names (Janus/MasterKey style dupes), entry_dos_times_constant (true when all 1980-01-01 = reproducible build). Also register the `dex.*` prebuilt fields under fmt apk with prefix `classes_dex_`.\"},\n {\"id\":\"aab-split-bundles\",\"concept\":\"Android App Bundle (.aab, protobuf manifest) and split-APK containers (.apks/.xapk/.apkm)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"fmt aab (alias android_bundle): zip with `base/manifest/AndroidManifest.xml` in aapt2 PROTOBUF (Resources.proto XmlNode{element=1 XmlElement{namespace_declaration=1, namespace_uri=2, name=3, attribute=4 XmlAttribute{namespace_uri=1,name=2,value=3,source=4,resource_id=5,compiled_item=6}, child=5}}) -- hand varint/length-delimited walk, no protobuf lib. Fields: package_name, version_code, version_name, min_sdk_version, module_names (`base`, feature dirs with `manifest/`), bundletool_version (BundleConfig.pb field bundletool{version=2} string), has_native_libs. fmt apks/xapk (alias split_apk): zip of `*.apk` (+ `toc.pb` for .apks; `manifest.json` for .xapk with package_name/version_code/version_name/split_apks[].id; `info.json` for .apkm): package_name (from manifest.json or base.apk AXML), split_names (JSON stored order), apk_member_names, base_apk_name. Route each inner APK to fmt apk.\"},\n {\"id\":\"software-packages\",\"concept\":\"Software/supply-chain packages: NuGet, Python wheel/sdist, npm tarball, Chrome CRX, VSIX\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"'Package Deal' pun read as software packages. Separate fmts: nupkg (alias nuget): zip with `*.nuspec` (XML ns varies) id, version, authors, description, dependencies (JSON id@range), tags; `[Content_Types].xml` + `_rels/.rels` + `package/services/metadata/core-properties/*.psmdcp` creator. wheel (aliases whl, python_wheel): `*.dist-info/METADATA` (RFC 822: Name, Version, Summary, Author, Requires-Dist JSON list), `WHEEL` (Wheel-Version, Generator, Root-Is-Purelib, Tag list), `RECORD` entry count / sha256 of a named file (urlsafe b64 no padding as stored), `entry_points.txt` console_scripts; sdist tar.gz `PKG-INFO`. npm (alias npm_tarball, tgz): gzip tar `package/package.json` name, version, main, scripts (JSON object; preinstall/postinstall = supply-chain cue), dependencies. crx (alias chrome_extension): `Cr24` @0, version u32 @4 (3), header_size u32 @8, CrxFileHeader protobuf (signed_header_data -> crx_id 16 B -> extension id = hex mapped a-p), then zip manifest.json name/version/manifest_version/permissions/host_permissions/background service_worker; vsix: `extension.vsixmanifest` Identity Id/Version/Publisher + `extension/package.json`. tarfile/zipfile/json/xml stdlib only.\"},\n {\"id\":\"apk-zip-structure\",\"concept\":\"APK/JAR zip-level forensics: signing-block offset, alignment, duplicate/hidden entries, LFH vs CD mismatches\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"fmt apk (+jar): cd_offset_u32_hex, signing_block_offset_u32_hex, eocd_comment_length, lfh_cd_name_mismatches (JSON), lfh_cd_method_mismatches, stored_entry_names, compressed_manifest (AndroidManifest method != 0), data_after_eocd_bytes, extra_field_ids_by_entry (zipalign pads with 0xd935 'Android alignment' extra), general_purpose_flags_union_u16_hex (encrypted bit trick 0x0001 on a non-encrypted APK = anti-analysis), entry_count_eocd vs entry_count_cd. Pure struct over PK\\\\x03\\\\x04 / PK\\\\x01\\\\x02 / PK\\\\x05\\\\x06.\"},\n {\"id\":\"android-backup-artifacts\",\"concept\":\"Android device artifacts: `.ab` backups, OBB, packages.xml / packages.list\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"fmt android_backup (alias ab): text header `ANDROID BACKUP\\\\n<version>\\\\n<compressed 0/1>\\\\n<encryption none|AES-256>\\\\n` then (zlib) tar with `apps/<pkg>/_manifest` (package, versionCode, platform version, signatures); fields backup_version, compressed, encryption, package_names (tar order), file_count. fmt packages_xml: ABX binary XML (`ABX\\\\0` magic, Android 12+) or text `<packages>`: package names, codePath, versionCode, installer, firstInstallTime (hex ms) -> utc; packages.list: name uid debuggable dataDir seinfo. fmt obb: zip/jobb footer.\"},\n {\"id\":\"mobileprovision-entitlements\",\"concept\":\"Standalone `.mobileprovision` / entitlements plists / iOS app extension Info.plists\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"fmt mobileprovision (alias provisioning_profile): CMS DER with an embedded XML plist (find `<?xml`..`</plist>`): team_identifier, team_name, app_id_name, application_identifier, uuid, name, creation_date_utc, expiration_date_utc, provisions_all_devices, provisioned_device_count, provisioned_devices (JSON stored order), entitlement_keys (sorted), get_task_allow, aps_environment, developer_certificate_sha1s (DER certs in DeveloperCertificates <data> base64 -> sha1 hex). Shares code with ios-ipa-identity; register also as ipa provision_* fields.\"},\n]\nfor g in new: assert g['id'] not in ids\n# insert new P1 at top, P2/P3 after existing P1 notes\np1=[g for g in new if g['priority']==1]; rest=[g for g in new if g['priority']!=1]\nold_p1=[g for g in gaps if g['priority']==1]; old_other=[g for g in gaps if g['priority']!=1]\nout=p1+old_p1+rest+old_other\nout.sort(key=lambda g:g['priority'])  # stable\ntxt='[\\n'+',\\n'.join('  '+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in out)+'\\n]'\njson.loads(txt)\ns=s[:m.start(1)]+txt+s[m.end(1):]\ns=s.replace(\"Ranking (D20 post-run): priority 1 = plausible D21-D23 question\",\"Ranking (D21 post-run): priority 1 = plausible D22-D24 question (mobile/package siblings of D21's APK)\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nst=json.load(open('.run/prebuild-state.json'))\nleft=[g['id'] for g in out if g['action']=='prebuild' and not (st.get('metadata-forensics:'+g['id'],{}).get('ok') or st.get('metadata-forensics:'+g['id'],{}).get('attempts',0)>=2)]\nprint(len(out),left)\nEOF\ngrep -n 'Ranking' reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md | cut -c1-200"}}}
