{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFTKEjfbzLC2rTY6nP2R","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both files are updated for day21. I didn't run tests, start any mode or submit anything.\n\n1. **`reference/techniques/metadata-forensics.md`** (now 235 lines):\n   - **Day 21 entry (\"Package Deal\"):** the field was `apk.package_name` for one 8,535-byte `mobile-001.apk`. The answer is the `<manifest package=…>` attribute copied as stored, not the app label or the filename. `aapt dump badging f.apk | head -1` gives it directly. The first submit was CORRECT in about 32 s. Time Trial (26 fields) and Mastery (130 fields) were both CORRECT first try, about 4–5 s in-window.\n   - **What was new:** the in-window field lookup in `lib.meta` had no `apk` format, so an LLM worker had to solve it. The synthesis question now lists five files, and every mode used the same APK.\n   - **Variant axes:** added these new values: field-set size 1/26/130, the plain format word `apk`, the five-file synthesis list, and the APK staying identical across modes. There was no `NOTES.md`, and the only variant cases were the two auto ones.\n   - **Other sections:** added an `apk.*` row to the recognition table and a rule for spelling Android identifiers. The Pitfalls section is compressed and gains a \"new container format needs its own format word\" lesson; day 20 is folded into the summary.\n\n2. **`reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md`:**\n   - Added a day21 forecast paragraph and atlas rows 129–136; `apk.package_name` is marked `seen D21`.\n   - Changed 31 rows from \"gap\" to \"prebuilt\", because the prebuild state file shows them as already built.\n   - The worker cue section is still exactly 60 lines; the JAR/APK cue line was rewritten in place.\n\n3. **Readiness gaps** (the JSON is still valid): every existing `prebuild` gap was already built, so I added 11 new ones.\n   - **Priority 1:** `apk-manifest-siblings`, `apk-signing-certs`, `apk-label-resources-arsc`, `apk-clone-rebuild-synthesis`, `ios-ipa-identity`.\n   - **Priority 2:** `apk-native-abis-dex`, `aab-split-bundles`, `software-packages`.\n   - **Priority 3:** `apk-zip-structure`, `android-backup-artifacts`, `mobileprovision-entitlements`.\n   - The day-20 Mach-O priority-1 gaps, all already built, moved down to priority 2.\n\n`lib/meta/apk.py` was not tracked by git when I wrote this; I assumed the lib worker is adding it. Both files point workers to it as the stdlib reader for the APK manifest, so check that it lands."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":911,"cache_read_input_tokens":129980,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":911},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9641bc75-74e7-43ea-9891-be166854c1b9","uuid":"c61f21ff-6e3d-4f90-bd6f-5bca6a2fe159","timestamp":"2026-10-21T13:23:29.823Z","request_id":"req_011CgFTKELMrn97KjipxBgv2"}
